 "cards": [
  {
   "dot": "cyan",
   "title": "Shapes to say out loud",
   "items": [
    "T = all tokens of all requests this step, concatenated (ragged, no padding)",
    "hidden 2048 = 32 query heads × 64; K/V use 8 heads (GQA, 4 q heads share one)",
    "Positions are per request, not indices into the flat batch",
    "Each layer: RMSNorm before attention and before the MLP"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "emerald",
   "title": "Where the cache is touched",
   "items": [
    "Each layer writes this step's K,V first, so a token attends to itself",
    "slot = block_id × 16 + offset, from BlockTable.slot_index",
    "Gather copies a request's scattered blocks back into token order"
   ]
  },
  {
   "dot": "amber",
   "title": "Why decode is memory-bound",
   "items": [
    "A decode step does 1 token of maths per request but reads all its KV and all weights",
    "Logits only at each request's last token: the 128256-wide head is costly"
   ]
  }
 ]
}